# Security baseline content requires security engineering review. This is the
# technical half of the change-control gate; the GitHub environment's required
# reviewers are the other half.
#
# Replace these placeholder teams with real ones before enabling branch
# protection, or the rules silently match nobody.

/ansible/roles/rhel8_stig_cat2/   @your-org/platform-security @your-org/linux-engineering
/ansible/controls/               @your-org/platform-security @your-org/isso
/scripts/stig/                   @your-org/platform-security
/.github/workflows/stig-*.yml    @your-org/platform-security @your-org/devops

# The AAP configuration decides who may run what, which controls need an
# approval node, and what is allowed to run on a schedule. A change here is a
# change to the enforcement of separation of duties.
/aap/                            @your-org/platform-security @your-org/aap-admins
/aap/controller/rbac.yml         @your-org/platform-security @your-org/isso

# Inventory group_vars decide which controls are on for which tier. A change
# here is a change to the security posture of a whole tier.
/ansible/inventory/group_vars/   @your-org/platform-security @your-org/isso
